  "reply": "No, The Indianapolis Star did not rely on multiple sources for the story about the 10-year-old girl who traveled for an abortion. According to the article \"In Rape Case, Politics Raced Ahead of News\" in the July 15, 2022 edition of The New York Times, the report in The Indianapolis Star \"relied on a single named source.\" The article notes that the facts were sparse and reporters struggled to confirm the story, which became a flash point in the national abortion debate.",
